## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of CORS risks and practical mitigations in a fintech SPA context, focusing on per-origin controls, token usage, and incident response.

## Key Concepts
- CORS headers and policies
- Token-based auth and JWTs
- CI/CD security checks for config
- Incident response for cross-origin abuse

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example snippet for server CORS config (pseudo)
const allowedOrigins = ['https://app.example.com','https://admin.app.example.com'];
app.use((req,res,next)=>{ 
  const origin = req.headers.origin;
  if (allowedOrigins.includes(origin)) { res.setHeader('Access-Control-Allow-Origin', origin);
     res.setHeader('Access-Control-Allow-Credentials','true');
     res.setHeader('Access-Control-Allow-Methods','GET,POST,OPTIONS');
  } else { res.status(403).send('origin not allowed'); }
  next();
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you automate detection of misconfig in CI?
- How would you validate that CORS policies don’t block legitimate cross-origin traffic?
